# Shapiro & Sutherland (1982) Table 1: polarized plane-parallel atmosphere.
#
# Emergent I(mu)/F and Q/I of a semi-infinite plane-parallel atmosphere with
# Thomson scattering: pure scattering (Chandrasekhar 1960, 11.7% at the limb)
# and two scattering-plus-absorption cases (lambda = 1/6, lambda = tau/(1+tau);
# Harrington 1969, u0 = h nu / k Teff = 20).  Each case is checked bin by bin
# against a deterministic solution (ReferenceTables.hpp, from
# planeparallel_reference.py), which itself reproduces the paper's pure
# scattering column to 2e-5.  One invocation runs all three cases, so the
# harness must see three PASS lines.
#
# One cell per layer with mirror side walls (every escaping photon counts) and
# the per-case default photon numbers: about 1.5M packets per generation for
# the scattering and lambda = 1/6 cases and 5M for lambda = tau/(1+tau), 32
# generations (~20 min on 16 ranks; the gate is 5 generation-scatter sigmas).
#
# Requires -DSTORM_MONTECARLO_POLARIZATION=ON.
TEST_ID="shapiro_sutherland_polarization"
TAGS="mpi"
CATEGORY="physics"
MPI_NP=16
RUN_ARGS=["--case", "all", "--generations", "32"]
CHECK_FUNCTION="check_shapiro_sutherland_polarization_case"
TIMEOUT=3600
